<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (4.2.1 Document Ingestion Pipeline)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1274 0 R
/E (The ingestion pipeline exists to turn uploaded engineering documents into structured, queryable knowledge without ever losing the trail back to the page a fact came from. A file enters as bytes and leaves as connected facts, and the path between is a sequence of decisions in which each one is forced by the problem the previous created.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1275 0 R
/E (Documents uploaded by users are first stored in MinIO object storage, while only the storage reference is passed through the Celery message broker to keep messages lightweight.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1276 0 R
/E (The ingestion service computes a content fingerprint to detect duplicate uploads, ensuring that identical documents are processed only once and avoiding unnecessary AI inference costs.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1277 0 R
/E (Based on the document type, files are routed into specialised extraction pipelines, including Work Order parsing, P&ID extraction using vision models, and LLM-based text extraction for manuals, reports, and emails.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1278 0 R
/E (Extracted entities, relationships, and provenance information are passed to an entity resolution stage, where different names referring to the same equipment are merged into a single canonical identifier.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1279 0 R
/E (Finally, a dedicated single graph writer batches updates into Neo4j, ensuring graph consistency, atomic version updates, and reliable downstream notifications.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1280 0 R
/E (Celery configurations such as acknowledgements, retries, execution time limits, and JSON-only serialization provide fault tolerance and secure distributed processing.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (4.2 Pipeline Implementation : Systems Engineering perspective )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (A retrieval technique becomes production-ready only when supported by robust systems engineering. PlantForge combines a knowledge graph built from plant documents, proactive event-driven agents, and a strict separation between graph-derived evidence and LLM-generated reasoning. Scalability and reliability are achieved through specialized worker pools, idempotent ingestion, serialized graph updates, fault-tolerant coordination, and concurrency driven by empirical load measurements. The following sections describe three core components: \(i\) the scalable document ingestion pipeline, \(ii\) the coordination architecture for distributed services, and \(iii\) the concurrent query-serving path designed to maintain consistent performance under multi-user workloads. Measurements and system limits are explicitly reported to characterize production behavior.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
