666 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (In Process Safety Management, minor engineering modifications can trigger complex secondary effects that lead to catastrophic accidents if their full blast radius is not understood. Operating as a digital process safety engineer, this service drafts the initial impact assessment for any proposed plant change by autonomously traversing the knowledge graph to discover what the target equipment is physically connected to, its historical failure modes, and any governing regulatory clauses. It then synthesizes this gathered context into a concise assessment that details how the modification affects the broader system and highlights specific secondary dependencies that must be evaluated. Maintaining a strict safety boundary, the system explicitly refuses to approve or reject the proposed change, instead functioning solely to provide comprehensive evidence and critical considerations for the human reviewer. This rigorous, graph-driven investigation accelerates the review process while significantly reducing the risk that engineers might overlook a hidden dependency.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
