686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 126 0 R
/E (A Permit-to-Work functions as the absolute last line of defense before a worker touches hazardous industrial equipment, demanding precise hazard mitigation over generic, copy-pasted templates. Triggered by a maintenance request, this life-critical service autonomously traverses the physical isolation boundary within the knowledge graph to identify every connected tag that must be secured, the required Lock-Out/Tag-Out \(LOTO\) methodology, and inherent dangers such as pressure or flammability. Synthesizing this data with the asset's failure history and governing procedures, the system generates a highly structured permit that details required personal protective equipment, compliance obligations, and specific pre-job briefing points. Refusing to rely on vague bureaucratic language, the generated narrative explicitly names the exact valves to lock and the precise procedures to follow. By grounding the permit creation in complete, real-time topological context, the system directly protects human lives while streamlining the administrative burden of hazard preparation.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
