741 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Technically, the contribution is treating a plant archive as a topology rather than a corpus. Multi-lane extraction preserves what flat parsing destroys; resolution and denoising make the graph coherent rather than confidently silent; and retrieval extends flow-based path pruning with degree dilution and provenance weighting, so ranking reflects both topological specificity and the reliability of the lane that produced each edge. Every answer is grounded against the evidence actually supplied, and engineer corrections enter the graph as structure letting the system unlearn bad source knowledge without retraining. It is also built to survive deployment: worker pools that scale on backlog, a serialised writer protecting a version guarantee, and measured concurrency work that removed twelve failures per hundred connections. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
742 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Commercially, the defensibility is the graph, not the model. Any competitor can call the same LLM; none can replicate a customer's twenty-year maintenance history, its resolved asset identities, or the corrections its own engineers have filed. That asset appreciates with every document ingested and transfers to no one.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
743 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (What the system deliberately does not do is decide. It drafts, assesses and flags and every output waits for a human signature. In an industry where approval is a legal act, that restraint is not a limitation of the product; it is the reason it can be deployed at all.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
